Part 1 implementation:

```rust
/// Parse effort from review input, reporting whether the user explicitly
/// selected an effort (flag or positional keyword).
///
/// Accepts `--quick`/`--thorough` flags anywhere in the input (existing
/// behavior), plus positional effort words as the *first* token: `quick`,
/// `normal`, `thorough` and synonyms `fast`/`light` → Quick, `deep`/`full`
/// → Thorough. Positional matching is first-token-only so file paths like
/// `src/deep/thing.rs` are never misread as an effort. Unknown words are
/// always content — never an error.
fn parse_review_effort_full(input: &str) -> (ReviewEffort, String, bool) {
    let mut effort = ReviewEffort::Normal;
    let mut explicit = false;
    let mut remaining_parts: Vec<&str> = Vec::new();

    for (i, part) in input.split_whitespace().enumerate() {
        match part {
            "--quick" => {
                effort = ReviewEffort::Quick;
                explicit = true;
            }
            "--thorough" => {
                effort = ReviewEffort::Thorough;
                explicit = true;
            }
            part if i == 0 => match effort_word(part) {
                Some(e) => {
                    effort = e;
                    explicit = true;
                }
                None => remaining_parts.push(part),
            },
            _ => remaining_parts.push(part),
        }
    }

    (effort, remaining_parts.join(" "), explicit)
}
```

And `effort_word`:

```rust
/// Map a positional word to an effort level, if it names one.
fn effort_word(word: &str) -> Option<ReviewEffort> {
    match word {
        "quick" | "fast" | "light" => Some(ReviewEffort::Quick),
        "normal" => Some(ReviewEffort::Normal),
        "thorough" | "deep" | "full" => Some(ReviewEffort::Thorough),
        _ => None,
    }
}
```

