Now, the code. Let me write `parse_review_effort` with a shared token matcher:

```rust
/// Map a single whitespace-delimited token to an effort level, if it names one.
///
/// Accepts both flags (`--quick`, `--thorough`) and natural positional words
/// (`quick`, `normal`, `thorough` plus `fast`, `deep`, `full`, `light`).
/// Unknown tokens return `None` — they are content (file path, range, `--pr`…),
/// never an error.
fn effort_for_token(token: &str) -> Option<ReviewEffort> {
    match token {
        "--quick" | "quick" | "fast" | "light" => Some(ReviewEffort::Quick),
        "--normal" | "normal" => Some(ReviewEffort::Normal),
        "--thorough" | "thorough" | "deep" | "full" => Some(ReviewEffort::Thorough),
        _ => None,
    }
}
```

